	D_q=\emptyset$. We thus assume that $q$ is above $\gamma_i'$ (see Fig.~\ref{fig:SearchInOneLowerEnvelope}, where $\gamma_i'$ is $\gamma_3'$). In this case, $p_i$
	is in $D_q$ and we report it. Next, starting from $\gamma_i'$, we traverse
	on the arcs of $\calU_1$ rightwards (resp., leftwards) until the distance
	between $q$ and the center of an arc is larger than $1$.
