and we use the retrieved schema to validate $J$.
The URI $u$ has, in general, the shape $\key{absURI}\catHash\key{f}$, where $\key{absURI}$ identifies a resource and
$\key{f}$ identifies a fragment inside the resource.
We do not formalize $\key{deref}(u)$, because the association between $\key{absURI}$ and the resource is
implementation dependent.
In this paper, we will only use references with shape $\#\key{f}$ (empty $\key{absURI}$).
