	\subsection{Solution of the homogenized problem}

	Numerical calculations are first performed for the local model. We obtain this model when the entire memory kernel is approximated by a delta function. In the limiting case $m=0$, from \eqref{3.10} we get the parabolic equation:
	\[
	(1 + r_0) \frac{\partial \widetilde{u}(x,t)}{\partial t} = \nabla \cdot \left(D \nabla \widetilde{u}(x,t)\right), \quad x \in \Omega,\ t > 0.
	\]
	In our case (see \eqref{3.9}):
	\[
	r_0 = (1-|Y_2|)^{-1} |Y_2| \approx 0.335697.
	\]

	In the domain $\Omega$, we construct a triangulation by first partitioning the square uniformly into smaller rectangles of equal size $h \times h$, and then dividing each rectangle into two right triangles using the diagonal from the bottom-left to the top-right vertex.
