However, in practice, citations are often unevenly distributed, with a small number of papers receiving a disproportionately large share of citations, while the majority receive far fewer– a phenomenon widely discussed as citation inequality~\citep{Garfield_1972,crespo_2013,nielsen_2021,dong_2021}.
